    },
    {
      "text": "Moving beyond Euclidean geometry is argued to be a necessity rather than an optional enhancement for maintaining the scaling law for next-generation foundation models.",
      "supported": true,
      "source_number": 1,
      "evidence_quote": "This position paper argues that moving beyond Euclidean geometry is not merely an optional enhancement but a necessity to maintain the scaling law for the next-generation of foundation models."
    },
    {
      "text": "Graph foundation models have shared substructures, including trees and cycles, underlying the graph domain.",
      "supported": true,
      "source_number": 2,
      "evidence_quote": "The key innovation is the discovery of a simple yet effective structural vocabulary of trees and cycles"
