      "text": "These graph substructures have an inherent connection to Riemannian geometry.",
      "supported": true,
      "source_number": 2,
      "evidence_quote": "we explore its inherent connection to Riemannian geometry."
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed integration strategies include fine-tuning, training from scratch, and hybrid approaches.",
      "supported": true,
      "source_number": 1,
      "evidence_quote": "we outline a roadmap for integrating non-Euclidean geometries into foundation models, including strategies for building geometric foundation models via fine-tuning, training from scratch, and hybrid approaches."
    },
    {
      "text": "Task-aware adaptability that dynamically reconfigures embeddings to match downstream application geometry is proposed to enhance efficiency and expressivity.",
      "supported": true,
      "source_number": 1,
      "evidence_quote": "Task-aware adaptability that dynamically reconfigures embeddings to match the geometry of downstream applications could further enhance efficiency and expressivity."
    },
    {
      "text": "Using non-Euclidean geometries could enable foundation models to leverage the relevant structures more efficiently.",
      "supported": true,
      "source_number": 1,
      "evidence_quote": "By adopting these geometries, foundation models could more efficiently leverage the aforementioned structures."
    },
    {
      "text": "RiemannGFM constructs a product bundle to incorporate diverse geometries of the structural vocabulary and stacks Riemannian layers in which the vocabulary is learned on a Riemannian manifold, offering cross-domain transferability.",
